    "summary": "Transcendent Here Comes Sunshine jam & killer Truckin' segues",
    "blurb": "The night shines with a soaring Here Comes Sunshine and an explosive second‑set sequence of Truckin' → Nobody's Fault But Mine → The Other One. Jerry’s guitar is on fire, Keith delivers a ridiculous post‑Truckin' keyboard outro, and the band locks in tight grooves throughout.",
    "review": "December 19, 1973 at Curtis Hixon Convention Hall captured one of the Dead’s late‑year high points. The first set rolls from solid roots numbers into a standout Here Comes Sunshine that many reviewers call transcendent – Jerry’s tone is “ear candy” and his solo lifts the whole band. The second set erupts with a seamless Truckin' → Nobody's Fault But Mine → The Other One medley, highlighted by Keith Godchaux’s wild keyboard outro after Truckin' and an earth‑shaking jam on The Other One that still rattles speakers today. Weather Report Suite rolls out with its classic Prelude/Part 1/Let It Grow flow, while Candyman and Stella Blue receive special praise for Jerry’s soaring wah‑heavy solo work. Across all six soundboard sources the recording is crisp, well‑balanced and faithful to the original two‑track tapes, making this the definitive version of a show that still feels fresh after fifty years.",
